# Searches in the mixin encoding of inheritance
# (corpora/contest_mixin_library.pl): scored points of the hard corpus,
# ported from the retired labeled points of contest_inheritance.pl,
# contest_inheritance_middle.pl, contest_inheritance_dynamic.pl and
# contest_inheritance_dynamic_middle.pl. Each asks whether a search
# reaches the Church true, boolean(true), as the labeled point did; the
# other answers of the search are the other branches' (false, or none),
# so these points are asked by membership, not whole.
#
# REACHABILITY. A graph is a module whose slots are its nodes' classes,
# and a node's hierarchy has one marker slot is_x for each node x of the
# graph, then reachable, next and two_hop: the labels of the labeled
# port are the positions of a fixed-width hierarchy. The class of node x
# implements is_x alone, the Church true, so that a union of node classes
# answers is_x when x's class is in the union. Its reachable is a class,
# the union of each successor's reachable and of the successor's class,
# the recursive branches first (the shape of the labeled rings); next is
# the union of the successors' classes, and two_hop is self.next.next.
# The test reads from.reachable.is_to, or a.two_hop.is_d.
# - contest_inheritance.pl's rings of 3, 20 and 40 nodes (does n0 reach
#   the last node?), the graph a -> b, b -> a, b -> c with each direct
#   successor first (does a reach c?), and the diamond a -> b, a -> c,
#   b -> d, c -> d (is d two hops from a?);
# - contest_inheritance_middle.pl's two rings, ring with a chord, lasso,
#   and ring with double successors.
#
# SUBSET SUM. The module has one class search_k for each level k = 0 .. n
# of the n items, whose hierarchy has accumulated and found; search_n's found is
# target.equality(self.accumulated), and search_k's found is the union of
# {search_(k+1), accumulated : self.accumulated}.found and
# {search_(k+1), accumulated : self.accumulated.plus(a_(k+1))}.found. The test reads
# {search_0, accumulated : 0}.found at church. The items are the first n odd
# primes and the target their total, reached only by taking every item.
#
# LONGEST COMMON SUBSEQUENCE, as a decision: the symbols a and b, the
# lists nil and cons (head, tail), and common_subsequence (left, right, need), whose
# found is true when need is zero, false when a list is empty, and
# otherwise the union of leaving out left's head, leaving out right's
# head and, when the heads are equal, leaving out both with need - 1. The
# strings are contest_inheritance_dynamic.pl's pseudo-random pair, need
# the length of their longest common subsequence.
#
# PROOF of each scored claim, a finite head: a finite sequence of choices
# reaches a yield equal to the Church true (the path to the target; the
# subset of every item; the matches of a longest common subsequence),
# whose test yields \a. a, and lambda beta eta with sets is consistent.
#
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - reachability: search with a set of visited nodes: J. Hopcroft, R.
#   Tarjan, Algorithm 447: Efficient Algorithms for Graph Manipulation, CACM
#   1973, doi:10.1145/362248.362272.
# - subset sum and longest common subsequence: dynamic programming: R.
#   Bellman, Dynamic Programming, Princeton University Press 1957; R. A.
#   Wagner, M. J. Fischer, The String-to-String Correction Problem, J. ACM
#   1974, doi:10.1145/321796.321811.
# - all three, reached from the definitions by tabled evaluation: W. Chen,
#   D. S. Warren, Tabled Evaluation with Delaying for General Logic
#   Programs, J. ACM 1996, doi:10.1145/227595.227597.

#   subset_point(?Point, ?Count): the first Count odd primes.
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_two") λ. integer 2)
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_four") λ. integer 4)
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_six") λ. integer 6)
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_eight") λ. integer 8)
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_ten") λ. integer 10)
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_twelve") λ. integer 12)
λ
. cons (λ_subset_point. _subset_point (text "mixin_subset_sum_sixteen") λ. integer 16) nil
